    "title": "SGA: Working Translation, Source-Repair, and Audit Drafts (SGA6 idx355 Source-Rescribe Checkpoint)",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21300786",
    "publication_date": "2026-07-10",
    "description": "<p>This is the reader-facing SGA working record for the Modern LaTeX Editions of Mathematics Manuscripts project. It retains the compact SGA5 and SGA6 reader-first surface and updates the front SGA6 French source-rescribe workpass to the frozen July 10 checkpoint through certification-ledger entry #352, scan idx355 / volume p342 / Exposé V p46.</p><p><strong>Open first:</strong> the SGA5 French workpass PDF, <code>01_SGA6_French_SourceRescribe_Workpass_NotCertified_idx355_20260710.pdf</code>, and the SGA6 English unsynchronized working-draft PDF. File <code>04_SGA6_TeX_SourceRescribe_Audit_NotCertified_idx355_20260710.zip</code> contains the editable French TeX, full certification and errata ledgers, compile logs, retained source crops, and a status README.</p><p><strong>What the source-rescribe found:</strong> the earlier repair033 branch was a readable scaffold with paraphrased and compressed regions. Direct scan work has restored omitted proofs and whole paragraphs, corrected mathematical relations and lambda/gamma notation, replaced an invented lemma statement, and removed unsupported equation tags. Nearby genuine tags were retained after individual comparison.</p><p><strong>Status:</strong> this is useful source-aware working material, not OCR-only, but it is not a critical edition, completed SGA6 release, whole-volume source-faithfulness certification, English synchronization, index audit, or publication-grade proofreading. SGA5 remains incomplete and SGA7 remains partial/caveat-heavy.</p><p>Corrections can be proposed through the GitHub mirror: <a href=\"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts\">https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts</a>.</p>",
